Requirements: 7   with obligations: 7

[task-01] A task file can carry an optional `## Context` section, for background that
    helps a reader understand the mandate but is not itself something the change must
    deliver: the problem being fixed, how the system behaves today, or measurements
    already taken.
    -> context-section-optional-background  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       A task file may carry an optional `## Context` section, and the system accepts
       task files both with and without it; the section is treated as background
       (problem being fixed, current behavior, measurements) and not as a deliverable of
       the change.

[task-02] Parsing a task file records the Context section as its own field, each block
    with its span back to the source. Context is not reported as unread source, and it
    is not a requirement: it gets no requirement id and no disposition, and adding or
    removing it does not move the mandate coverage counts.
    -> parse-records-context-field  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Parsing a task file records the Context section as its own field on the parsed
       task-file result, separate from the requirement sections and other fields.
    -> context-blocks-carry-source-spans  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The Context field recorded by parsing a task file holds its content as blocks,
       and each block carries a span that points back to its location in the source task
       file.
    -> context-not-reported-unread  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Context section content is not reported as unread source: when a task file is
       parsed and the unread-source report is produced, the Context section's blocks do
       not appear in it.
    -> context-blocks-have-no-requirement-id-or-disposition  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Context section blocks are recorded without requirement ids and without
       dispositions: parsing a task file assigns no requirement id to any Context block
       and produces no disposition for it.
    -> context-does-not-move-coverage-counts  [invariant/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Mandate coverage counts are independent of the Context section: adding or
       removing Context blocks leaves the coverage counts identical.

[task-03] Decomposition shows the context to the model, labelled as context and kept
    apart from the list of requirements, so the model can use the background without
    being asked to account for it. A task file with no Context section produces exactly
    the same model requests and the same results as it does today.
    -> context-shown-labelled-and-separate  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Decomposition presents the task file's context to the model labelled as context
       and kept apart from the list of requirements.
    -> context-not-an-accountable-requirement  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The context background supplied to the model is used as background only: the
       model is not asked to account for it, so no obligation or disposition is required
       of the model for the context content.
    -> no-context-task-file-unchanged-behavior  [regression/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Preserve the existing behavior for a task file with no Context section: it
       produces exactly the same model requests and the same results as before this
       change.

